Fudan University, Shanghai 200031, China."},{"affiliation":"Shanghai Key Laboratory of Gene Editing and Cell Therapy for Rare Diseases, Fudan University, Shanghai 200031, China."},{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Brain Function and Disorders and MOE Frontiers Center for Brain Science, Fudan University, Shanghai 200032, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhang H","lastName":"Zhang","firstName":"Hongbo","initials":"H","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1071-4416"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Joint Centre of Translational Medicine, The First Affiliated Hospital of Wenzhou Medical University, Wenzhou, Zhejiang 325015, China."},{"affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Sciences Laboratory, Åbo Akademi University, 20520 Turku, Finland."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9074-9450"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1071-4416"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"4","volume":"36","journalIssueId":4019543,"dateOfPublication":"2025 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2025,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Mol Ther Nucleic Acids","title":"Molecular therapy. Nucleic acids","essn":"2162-2531","issn":"2162-2531","nlmid":"101581621","isoabbreviation":"Mol Ther Nucleic Acids"},"printPublicationDate":"2025-12-01"},"pubYear":"2025","pageInfo":"102737","abstractText":"mRNA-driven CRISPR-Cas9 gene therapies have garnered widespread attention due to their ability to maintain highly efficient editing activity while preventing integration into the host cell genome. However, the widespread clinical application of mRNA-driven CRISPR-Cas9 gene therapy is limited by mRNA instability, strong immune responses, a short half-life, inefficient delivery <i>in vivo</i>, and off-target effects. This review summarizes recent advancements in efforts to enhance mRNA stability and translation efficiency, and it describes novel delivery vectors currently being used for mRNA-driven CRISPR-Cas9 therapies. Moreover, the development of novel gene editors based on CRISPR-Cas9 engineering and the development of length fragment integration technology based on prime editing tool engineering are also discussed. The discussion of these advances aims to provide a full picture of the challenges of mRNA-based CRISPR-Cas9 therapeutics for the treatment of various diseases.","affiliation":"Joint Centre of Translational Medicine, The First Affiliated Hospital of Wenzhou Medical University, Wenzhou, Zhejiang 325015, China.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic-eCollection","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"82201287","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"82225014","orderIn":0},{"agency":"China Sponsorship Council","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"82171148","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Science and Technology Commission of Shanghai Municipality","grantId":"23J31900100","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"82372145","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Research Council of Finland","grantId":"347897","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Natural Science Foundation of Zhejiang Province","grantId":"LBD24H180001","orderIn":0},{"agency":"China Scholarship Council","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Shanghai Municipal Education Commission","grantId":"2023ZKZD12","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Natural Science Foundation of Zhejiang Province","grantId":"BD24H180004","orderIn":0}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Gene therapy","Crispr-cas9","Delivery Vectors","Mt: Rna/Dna Editing","Engineering To Mrna","Length Fragment Integration Technology"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.omtn.