ata M, Shida Y, Ogasawara W, Yamazaki H, Takaku H.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Sato R","lastName":"Sato","firstName":"Rikako","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Applied Life Sciences, Niigata University of Pharmacy and Medical and Life Sciences, Akiha-ku, Niigata 956-8603, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Maruyama K","lastName":"Maruyama","firstName":"Kaito","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Applied Life Sciences, Niigata University of Pharmacy and Medical and Life Sciences, Akiha-ku, Niigata 956-8603, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Ara S","lastName":"Ara","firstName":"Satoshi","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Research Institute for Creating the Future, FUJI OIL Co., Ltd, Tsukubamirai-shi, Ibaraki 300-2497, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Shibata M","lastName":"Shibata","firstName":"Masayuki","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Research Institute for Creating the Future, FUJI OIL Co., Ltd, Tsukubamirai-shi, Ibaraki 300-2497, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Shida Y","lastName":"Shida","firstName":"Yosuke","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Bioengineering, Nagaoka University of Technology, Nagaoka, Niigata 940-2188, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Ogasawara W","lastName":"Ogasawara","firstName":"Wataru","initials":"W","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Bioengineering, Nagaoka University of Technology, Nagaoka, Niigata 940-2188, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Yamazaki H","lastName":"Yamazaki","firstName":"Harutake","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Applied Life Sciences, Niigata University of Pharmacy and Medical and Life Sciences, Akiha-ku, Niigata 956-8603, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Takaku H","lastName":"Takaku","firstName":"Hiroaki","initials":"H","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3785-8030"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Applied Life Sciences, Niigata University of Pharmacy and Medical and Life Sciences, Akiha-ku, Niigata 956-8603, Japan."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3785-8030"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"26","journalIssueId":4084569,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Jan","monthOfPublication":1,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"FEMS Yeast Res","title":"FEMS yeast research","essn":"1567-1364","issn":"1567-1356","nlmid":"101085384","isoabbreviation":"FEMS Yeast Res"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-01-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"foag014","abstractText":"Lipomyces starkeyi is a promising oleaginous yeast with industrial potential. However, its genome engineering remains constrained by low gene-targeting efficiency and the requirement for long homologous regions. Herein, we established a CRISPR/Cas9 genome-editing platform for L. starkeyi by expressing codon-optimized Streptococcus pyogenes Cas9 fused to an SV40 nuclear localization signal. Furthermore, in vitro-transcribed single-guide RNAs (sgRNAs) were directly delivered into the host, eliminating the need for endogenous RNA polymerase III-dependent sgRNA expression. CRISPR/Cas9 activity was validated using a codon-optimized Aequorea coerulescens GFP reporter. Cas9-induced frameshift mutations caused GFP disruption, leading to fluorescence loss. Gene replacement at the LsURA3 locus was evaluated using donor constructs with homologous regions ranging from 50-3000 bp. In a Cas9-expressing wild-type background, precise gene replacement was dependent on homology arm length, increasing from 36% with 50-bp arms to 80% with 3000-bp arms. Notably, in a Cas9-expressing Δlslig4 strain with suppressed non-homologous end joining (NHEJ), precise gene replacement was achieved with 100% accuracy using 50-bp homology arms under CRISPR/Cas9-dependent conditions. Together, these results demonstrate that a Pol III-independent CRISPR/Cas9 system combined with NHEJ suppression enables precise genome editing in L. starkeyi, providing a foundation for functional genomics and metabolic engineering.","affiliation":"Department of Applied Life Sciences, Niigata University of Pharmacy and Medical and Life Sciences, Akiha-ku, Niigata 956-8603, Japan.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"JSPS","grantId":"25K08907","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Japan Science and Technology Agency","grantId":"JPMJPF2211","orderIn":0},{"agency":"New Energy and Industrial Technology Development Organization","orderIn":0},{"agency":"JSPS","grantId":"25K18164","orderIn":0},{"agency":"JSPS","grantId":"JPJS00420240017","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Streptococcus pyogenes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Gene Targeting","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Lipomyces","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["LiPomyces starkeyi","Homologous Recombination","Nonhomologous End Joining","Genome Editing","Crispr/cas9","Oleaginous Yeast"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","