PMC13522793","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13522793"]},"doi":"10.1016/j.xcrm.2026.102940","title":"CRISPR-Cas9-producing probiotic bacteria for editing NOX2/gp91&lt;sup&gt;phox&lt;/sup&gt; and treating inflammatory bowel disease.","authorString":"Zhang C, Li T, Hao H, Wang G, Zhang Y, Huang Y, Chen L, Wang J, Yang XJ, Bi X.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Zhang C","lastName":"Zhang","firstName":"Chen","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Li T","lastName":"Li","firstName":"Tianyu","initials":"T","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Hao H","lastName":"Hao","firstName":"Huoye","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang G","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Gang","initials":"G","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhang Y","lastName":"Zhang","firstName":"Yuzhe","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Huang Y","lastName":"Huang","firstName":"Yue","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Chen L","lastName":"Chen","firstName":"Lili","initials":"L","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang J","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Jin","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Yang XJ","lastName":"Yang","firstName":"Xiang-Jiao","initials":"XJ","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Rosalind and Morris Goodman Cancer Institute & Department of Medicine, McGill University, Montreal, QC H3A 1A3, Canada."}]}},{"fullName":"Bi X","lastName":"Bi","firstName":"Xiuli","initials":"X","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China; Key Laboratory for Chronic Diseases Molecular Mechanism Research and Nutritional Intervention of Shenyang, Shenyang 110036, China. Electronic address: xiulibi@lnu.edu.cn."}]}}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"8","volume":"7","journalIssueId":4244813,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Cell Rep Med","title":"Cell reports. Medicine","essn":"2666-3791","issn":"2666-3791","nlmid":"101766894","isoabbreviation":"Cell Rep Med"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-08-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"102940","abstractText":"The primary pathogenic mechanism of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) involves elevated levels of reactive oxide species (ROS) in the gut, leading to oxidative stress and damage to the intestinal barrier function. We engineered a non-pathogenic bacterial strain, Escherichia coli Nissle 1917 (EcN), for oral CRISPR-Cas9 delivery to edit NOX2 (encoding the gp91<sup>phox</sup> subunit of NADPH oxidase 2), thereby alleviating IBD symptoms by reducing ROS. EcN expressing the Cas9/sgRNA ribonucleoprotein (RNP) was encapsulated in a hydrogel (composed of hyaluronic acid, chitosan, and MgCl<sub>2</sub>), which protected EcN-RNP from degradation and increased survival from 0.07% to 12%. EcN-RNP hydrogel reduced NOX2 expression by 47% and ROS by 88% in lipopolysaccharide-induced RAW264.7 cells. Moreover, oral delivery of EcN-RNP hydrogel mitigated inflammation in dextran sodium sulfate-induced colitis mouse models. Mechanistically, the hydrogel could activate the NRF2-HO1/GPX4 pathway by inhibiting NOX2 expression, enhancing oxidative defense, and promoting glutathione accumulation. Thus, the EcN-RNP hydrogel offers a promising therapeutic strategy for IBD.","affiliation":"College of Life Science, Liaoning University, Shenyang 110036, China.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Department of Science &amp; Technology of Liaoning Province","grantId":"2024-BSLH-103","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Liaoning Province Educational Department","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"32501261","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice, Inbred C57BL"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Escherichia coli","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Colitis","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CI","qualifierName":"chemically induced"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Inflammatory Bowel Diseases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Disease Models, Animal"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Reactive Oxygen Species","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"