of Human Disease Comparative Medicine, Institute of Laboratory Animal Sciences, Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences and Comparative Medicine Center, Peking Union Medical College, Beijing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Xu X","lastName":"Xu","firstName":"Xueling","initials":"X","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0007-6831-6756"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"College of Bee Science and Biomedicine, Fujian Agriculture and Forestry University, Fuzhou, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Li P","lastName":"Li","firstName":"Pan","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Xianghu Laboratory, Hangzhou, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Fang Y","lastName":"Fang","firstName":"Yi","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Key Lab of Animal Production, Product Quality and Security, Ministry of Education, Jilin Agricultural University, Changchun, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Deng S","lastName":"Deng","firstName":"Shoulong","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"National Center of Technology Innovation for Animal Model, National Human Diseases Animal Model Resource Center, National Health Commission of China (NHC) Key Laboratory of Human Disease Comparative Medicine, Institute of Laboratory Animal Sciences, Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences and Comparative Medicine Center, Peking Union Medical College, Beijing, China."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0004-8984-0045"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0007-6831-6756"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"6","volume":"8","journalIssueId":3967318,"dateOfPublication":"2025 Jun","monthOfPublication":6,"yearOfPublication":2025,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Animal Model Exp Med","title":"Animal models and experimental medicine","essn":"2576-2095","issn":"2096-5451","nlmid":"101726292","isoabbreviation":"Animal Model Exp Med"},"printPublicationDate":"2025-06-01"},"pubYear":"2025","pageInfo":"1004-1022","abstractText":"Cell lineage tracing is a key technology for describing the developmental history of individual progenitor cells and assembling them to form a lineage development tree. However, traditional methods have limitations of poor stability and insufficient resolution. As an efficient and flexible gene editing tool, CRISPR-Cas9 system has been widely used in biological research. Furthermore, CRISPR-Cas9 gene editing-based tracing methods can introduce fluorescent proteins, reporter genes, or DNA barcodes for high-throughput sequencing, enabling precise lineage analysis, significantly improving precision and resolution, and expanding its application range. In this review, we summarize applications of CRISPR-Cas9 system in cell lineage tracing, with special emphasis on its successful applications in traditional model animals (e.g., zebrafish and mice), large animal models (pigs), and human cells or organoids. We also discussed its potential prospects and challenges in xenotransplantation and regenerative medicine.","affiliation":"College of Animal Science and Technology, China Agricultural University, Beijing, China.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Institute of Laboratory Animal Sciences, Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences and Comparative Medicine Center, Peking Union Medical College, Collaborative Innovation Program of the Chinese Academy of Sciences","grantId":"22SH19","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Non-profit Central Research Institute Fund of Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","grantId":"2023-PT180-01","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Zebrafish"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descripto